you need:
 node.js 18+
 microsoft excel
 windows
 vs code

start dev:
 Unzip the archive in any convenient location (I placed it in the root of the system drive).
 Open PowerShell or cmd and navigate to the project directory (C:/vba-cli)

 Run the following commands:
  npm install
  npm link

 After that, the vba command will be available globally.
  To check that everything worked, write “vba help” or “vba -v” in Powershell.
   It should display a list of commands or the version.

 Then go to you VBA projects dir and execute the command:
  "vba init <name>" ("vba init testProject")

 your vs code will be redirect you to new window in new project

 Then execute in Powershell "vba dev"
  Changes to each VBA file will be automatically saved to the Excel file in the project root, like Live Server for JS.
